          "secNumber": "6.3",
          "heading": "Laboratory and field interpretation",
          "content": "## Laboratory and field interpretation\n\nA coastal stair tower will experience spray and intermittent wetting. Compare two concretes with equal target strength but different binder systems. Develop an exposure map and identify where chloride transport, carbonation, cracking and workmanship may dominate. Use illustrative profiles to define measurements for trial mixes, but do not compute service life without calibrated input and suitable acceptance framework.\n\nThe experiments in this unit deliberately distinguish physical observation from a mathematical surrogate. Before using a laboratory to defend a structural or construction decision, document the material source, temperatures, specimen dimensions, test method, reference basis and limitations of calibration. Record negative results and unexpected trends: such outcomes are often more informative than a tidy curve that happens to fit the assumed model."
